## Company Overview

Founded in 2016 by Charity Majors and Christine Yen (engineers from Parse and Google), headquartered in San Francisco. Venture‑backed, globally distributed team. Honeycomb was created to solve the problem of traditional monitoring and APM tools failing under the complexity of modern, distributed production systems.

## How It Works

- Unified event‑based data model
- [OpenTelemetry](https://www.honeycomb.io/resources/getting-started/getting-started-with-opentelemetry)‑native ingestion and instrumentation
- Built for high‑cardinality, high‑dimensional data
- Fast query engine optimized for exploratory workflows
- Designed for complex, distributed systems

## Core Capabilities

- Real‑time querying and visualization
